Deleting 3 from the tree built by `5 3 6 2 4 7`:

```text
      5                5
     / \              / \
    3   6     →      4   6
   / \   \          /     \
  2   4   7        2       7
```

3 has two children. Its successor is 4 (the leftmost node of its right subtree). Copy 4 into the node, then delete the old 4, a leaf. Preorder: `5 4 2 6 7`.

```cpp
Node* del(Node* node, long long key) {
    if (!node) return nullptr;
    if (key < node->key) node->left = del(node->left, key);
    else if (key > node->key) node->right = del(node->right, key);
    else if (!node->left) return node->right;        // zero or one child
    else if (!node->right) return node->left;
    else {
        Node* succ = node->right;
        while (succ->left) succ = succ->left;
        node->key = succ->key;
        node->right = del(node->right, succ->key);
    }
    return node;
}
```
